cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the specific work you used, not this repository. The reproduced works
  are by Asadullah Ali Al-Andalusi, founder of The Andalusian Project, and
  copyright in them is his (or, for journal and conference papers, his and his
  co-authors' and the publishers'); this repository does not relicense them and
  grants nothing over them. The CC BY-NC 4.0 licence below covers the archive's
  own material only - its data files, scripts, site source and documentation.
  Where an original host is gone, cite the archive's copy and name the Wayback
  capture it came from. See NOTICE.md, which lists every withheld item.
type: dataset
title: "The Andalusian Project Archive"
abstract: >-
  A preservation record of the published written and spoken work of Asadullah Ali
  Al-Andalusi ("The Andalusian Project"), assembled by archival recovery in 2026
  after the original web presence was lost, and catalogued with per-item
  provenance. The corpus is partial and the record says so: of 72 catalogued
  written works, 47 have full text in the repository, 24 are catalogued as
  Wayback-only with no text held, and 1 is unrecovered; 7 published post pages
  hold partial captures that no lane was able to improve. Recovered prose is
  reproduced verbatim, never summarised, paraphrased or merged. This record
  preserves what was published and then lost. It takes no position on the claims
  it preserves, and it is not an endorsement of them.
